      },
      "lineNbr": 459,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-21T22:20:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I initially considered doing this but then decided that it\u0027s probably better to disallow PipelineDataGatherer/UniformManager from being in an invalid state. So having a default value passed in via ctor doesn\u0027t hurt even though it will always get overwritten the way this code interacts with `gatherer`.\n\nI think a better abstraction is to remove the layout state mutation altogether and really allow a UniformManager to be lightweight and use one-off short-lived instances. That will make it easier to reason about its state if code deep-down the stack can\u0027t arbitrary reset a gatherer. Perhaps a candidate for another pass in a follow-up?",
